FPS Overlay - third-party components and credits
=================================================

This project builds on great open-source work by others. The MIT license
of FPS Overlay covers only this project's own code (main.py, overlay_window.py,
fps_worker.py, config.py, autostart.py, build scripts), not the components
listed below.

PresentMon
----------
File:      PresentMon-2.5.1-x64.exe (bundled with the app and inside FpsOverlay.exe)
Author:    Intel Corporation / GameTechDev
License:   MIT License
Source:    https://github.com/GameTechDev/PresentMon

The heart of the measurement: reads real frame Present() timings via ETW.
FPS Overlay merely parses its CSV output - all credit for the hard part
goes to the PresentMon team.

PyQt6
-----
Author:    Riverbank Computing Ltd
License:   GPL v3 (commercial license available from Riverbank)
Website:   https://www.riverbankcomputing.com/software/pyqt/

Powers the transparent always-on-top overlay window, the settings menu,
and the color/font pickers. NOTE: because the released FpsOverlay.exe
bundles PyQt6, that binary is distributed under the terms of the GNU GPL v3;
the source code in this repository remains MIT-licensed.

psutil
------
Author:    Giampaolo Rodola
License:   BSD 3-Clause
Source:    https://github.com/giampaolo/psutil

Used to resolve foreground window process names and filter system processes.

Microsoft / Windows internals
-----------------------------
Thanks to the Microsoft documentation community for the DWM attributes
